PROJECT DEVELOPMENT
The research fork adds full-key identity checks for the 9x9 representation,
bounded/checkpointed experiment drivers, cancellation and shutdown fixes,
and an optional sufficient pairing-bound oracle. Separate project tools
include horizon minimax, proof-number search, independent certificate
checkers, exhaustive response-family replay, cache reconciliation, and the
LaTeX developmental research note. Packaging adds a reproducible verifier,
a CI workflow template, release metadata, and documentation.

ASSISTANCE AND CLAIMS
Development used AI-assisted implementation, mathematical exploration, and
proof drafting. The project does not claim that the 9x9 opening is solved,
that its results are literature-first, or that its manuscript is peer-reviewed
or proof-assistant verified. Separate verification implementations should not
be confused with independent external review.
